{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776024228,"nonce":"HcnWNVHGGd+pZHd/ISuomkXBZeo=","title":"auth-merge fallback dirty check treats untracked files as dirty","message":"The `pre-auth-check` path resolution in `cli/auth-merge.sh:592` uses a relative path (`../../../../bin/pre-auth-check`) that resolves to `/Users/mll/Main/bin/pre-auth-check` instead of `~/.dotfiles/bin/pre-auth-check`. This causes the fallback dirty-check code path to run, which uses raw `git status --porcelain` and treats ALL untracked files as dirty.\n\nThe proper `pre-auth-check` script (line 214-221) already handles this correctly — it only blocks on staged changes and explicitly ignores untracked files.\n\n**Fix:** The `pre-auth-check` lookup should use `command -v pre-auth-check` or `which pre-auth-check` to find it on PATH, rather than a fragile relative path from the script location.\n\n**Impact:** Any repo with untracked files (normal for a vault/notes repo) cannot complete auth merges without stashing first.","files":null}]}